INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4900932001030129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Basics of Electronics Engineering involves the syllabus topic  types of semiconductor.  p-n junction diode formation and characteristics.  applicat as applied within Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Explain how  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applicat applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Basics of Electronics Engineering involves the syllabus topic  pnp and npn transistors as applied within Transistor characteristics and biasing 10. Explain how  PNP and NPN transistors applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Basics of Electronics Engineering involves the syllabus topic  common emitter amplifier.  common collector amplifier  multistage amplifier as applied within Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5. Explain how  Common emitter amplifier.  Common collector amplifier  Multistage amplifier applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Basics of Electronics Engineering involves the syllabus topic  jfet and mosfet  special purpose diode as applied within Special purpose diode and Applications 5. Explain how  JFET and MOSFET  Special purpose diode applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applicat appears in “Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to  Types of semiconductor.  P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.  Applications - Diode as rectifier, half wave, full wave and bridge rectifier.  Need of filters.  C, π filters., Semiconductor diode characteristics and its Applications 5.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  PNP and NPN transistors appears in “Transistor characteristics and biasing 10”. Define its role and features, relate it to conduction through transistor leakage current, relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to conduction through transistor leakage current, relationship between α and β.  Transistor configuration & characteristics for CB, CC.  Load line and biasing methods of transistor., Transistor characteristics and biasing 10. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  Common emitter amplifier.  Common collector amplifier  Multistage amplifier appears in “Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Transistor as an amplifier: 2.5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):**  JFET and MOSFET  Special purpose diode appears in “Special purpose diode and Applications 5”. Define its role and features, relate it to Zener diode & it''s application,  Photo diode  LDR  Photovoltaic Cell  Light Emitting Diode  Varactor Diode  Digital Display, Special purpose diode and Applications 5, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Zener diode & it''s application,  Photo diode  LDR  Photovoltaic Cell  Light Emitting Diode  Varactor Diode  Digital Display, Special purpose diode and Applications 5. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Basics of Electronics Engineering task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

